{#
  robots.txt — generated, not hand-maintained.

  Search and AI crawlers must NOT be blocked (spec §10, §11). OAI-SearchBot is
  named explicitly because OpenAI's publisher documentation states that blocking
  it removes the site from ChatGPT Search citations — the opposite of the goal.

  GROUPING SEMANTICS (fixed after a live audit found /admin/ wasn't actually
  disallowed for these three crawlers): per the Robots Exclusion Protocol, a
  crawler that matches a specific named User-agent group (Googlebot, Bingbot,
  OAI-SearchBot) uses ONLY that group's own rules -- it does not also pick up
  Disallow lines from a separate `User-agent: *` group, even one further down
  the file. Each named group below therefore repeats its own Disallow:
  /admin/ rather than relying on the wildcard group to cover it.

  Non-production builds disallow everything. An indexable staging site is an SEO
  incident, and this makes that impossible by default rather than by remembering
  (spec §15).
#}
{%- if site.indexable -%}
# {{ company.brand }} — {{ site.url }}

User-agent: *
Allow: /
Disallow: /admin/

# Search crawlers — explicitly permitted. Each repeats Disallow: /admin/
# because a named group does not inherit rules from User-agent: * above.
User-agent: Googlebot
Allow: /
Disallow: /admin/

User-agent: Bingbot
Allow: /
Disallow: /admin/

# AI search. Blocking this removes the site from ChatGPT Search citations.
User-agent: OAI-SearchBot
Allow: /
Disallow: /admin/

Sitemap: {{ site.url }}/sitemap.xml
{%- else -%}
# Non-production build ({{ site.env }}). Indexing disabled.
User-agent: *
Disallow: /
{%- endif %}
